hadiths[74]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1754","Sidna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, says that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Of all the people, who has the greatest right over me for good companionship?"" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, replied, ""Your mother."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, ""Then your mother."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, ""Then your mother."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, ""Then your father."" (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, gave precedence to the mother because the mother endures much hardship with the child: carrying him for nine months, then giving birth, then nursing, then raising, caring during illness and distress.)"
"1755","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: No child spoke in the cradle except for three children. One was ‘Isa (peace be upon him), the second was the companion of Jurayj. And Jurayj was a devout worshipper who built a place of worship and lived in it. He was praying when his mother came and called him, “O Jurayj!” He thought to himself, “O Allah, my mother is calling me and I am in prayer (should I continue praying or respond to my mother)?” In the end, he remained in prayer, so his mother went back. The next day, she came again and called, “O Jurayj!” He said, “O Allah, my mother is calling me and I am in prayer.” Again, he remained in prayer. On the third day, his mother came and called, but Jurayj remained in prayer, so his mother said, “O Allah, do not let him die until he sees the faces of immoral women (i.e., until he is confronted by them).” Then the Children of Israel began to talk about Jurayj and his worship. Among the Children of Israel was a prostitute whose beauty was proverbial. She said, “If you wish, I will put Jurayj to trial.” Then the woman went before Jurayj, but he paid her no attention. Eventually, she went to a shepherd who used to take refuge in Jurayj’s place of worship, and she allowed him to have relations with her, so he did, and she became pregnant by him. When she gave birth to the child, she said, “This child is from Jurayj.” Hearing this, the people came to him, brought him down, destroyed his place of worship, and began to beat him. He said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “You committed adultery with this prostitute, and she has given birth to your child.” Jurayj said, “Where is the child?” They brought the child, so Jurayj said, “Let me pray.” Then he prayed, came to the child, poked him in the stomach, and said, “O child, who is your father?” The child said, “So-and-so, the shepherd.” Hearing this, the people rushed to Jurayj, kissing and caressing him, and said, “We will rebuild your place of worship with gold and silver.” He said, “No, rebuild it as it was, with clay.” So they rebuilt it. (The third) was a child among the Children of Israel who was suckling from his mother when a well-dressed, handsome rider passed by. His mother, seeing him, said, “O Allah, make my son like this rider.” Upon hearing this, the child left his mother’s breast, looked at the rider, and said, “O Allah, do not make me like him.” After saying this, he returned to suckling. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “It is as if I am seeing the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at that moment, showing with his finger how the boy began to suckle again.” Then a slave woman passed by whom people were beating and saying, “You have committed adultery and theft.” She was saying, “Allah is sufficient for me, and He is my guardian.” So his mother said, “O Allah, do not make my son like her.” Hearing this, the child again left suckling, looked at the woman, and said, “O Allah, make me like her.” At that time, a conversation took place between the mother and the child. The mother said, “O shaven-headed one! When a handsome man passed by and I said, ‘O Allah, make my son like him,’ you said, ‘O Allah, do not make me like him.’ And when the slave woman, whom people were beating and accusing of adultery and theft, passed by, I said, ‘O Allah, do not make my son like her,’ you said, ‘O Allah, make me like her.’ (What is the matter?)” The child replied, “That rider was a tyrant, so I prayed, ‘O Allah, do not make me like him.’ And as for the slave woman, people were falsely accusing her, saying she committed adultery and theft, though she had done neither, so I said, ‘O Allah, make me like her.’”"
"1756","‘Abdullah bin ‘Amr bin al-‘As (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “I pledge allegiance to you for migration and jihad, seeking reward from Allah.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: “Are either of your parents alive?” He replied: “Both are alive.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: “Do you seek reward from Allah?” He replied: “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Then return to your parents and treat them kindly.”"
"1757","Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Indeed, Allah the Exalted has made disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive (as the disbelievers used to do), not giving (to whom it is due while having wealth), and asking (for that which one has no right to ask) forbidden for you. And He dislikes three things (though they are not as sinful as the first three): useless talk, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."
"1758","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May his nose be rubbed in dust, may his nose be rubbed in dust, may his nose be rubbed in dust."" It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Whose?"" He said: ""The one who finds his parents, both of them or one of them, in old age, and then does not enter Paradise (by serving them)."""
"1759","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that when he would go to Makkah, he would keep a donkey with him for recreation, and when he would get tired from riding the camel, he would ride on it, and he would keep a turban which he would tie on his head. One day, he was going on the donkey when suddenly a Bedouin appeared. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Are you not so-and-so, the son of so-and-so?"" He replied, ""Yes."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him the donkey and said, ""Ride on it,"" and also gave him the turban and said, ""Tie it on your head."" Some of Sayyiduna Abdullah's companions said, ""You have given away your recreational donkey and the turban which you used to tie on your head. May Allah forgive you."" He said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'The greatest act of goodness is that a person treats his father's friends well after his father's death.' And this Bedouin's father was a friend of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1760","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: A woman came to me with her two daughters. She asked me (for something), but I had nothing except one date, so I gave it to her. She took the date, split it into two pieces, and gave one piece to each of her daughters, and she herself did not eat anything. Then she got up and left. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came, so I told him about this woman. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever is tested with daughters (i.e., raises them, teaches them religion, and marries them to a righteous person), then on the Day of Resurrection, they will become a shield for him from Hell."
"1761","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever raises two girls until they reach maturity, then on the Day of Resurrection, I and he will come like this—and he (peace be upon him) joined his fingers together (meaning, on the Day of Resurrection, he will be with me). A Muslim should, if he has daughters himself, do good to them; otherwise, he should raise two orphan girls and, when they reach maturity, arrange their marriage, so that he may attain the companionship of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1762","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""Whoever wishes that his provision be increased and his life be prolonged, then he should maintain his ties (i.e., treat his relatives well)."""
"1763","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have some relatives with whom I maintain ties, but they cut me off. I do good to them, but they do evil to me. I show patience, but they act ignorantly towards me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you are truly as you say, then it is as if you are throwing hot ashes on their faces, and there will always remain with you an angel from Allah who will support you against them as long as you remain in that state."""
"1764","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah the Exalted created the creation, and when He finished making them, the tie of kinship stood up and said, ""This is the place of one who seeks refuge from being cut off."" (That is, by the tongue of its state, or an angel spoke on its behalf, and this is an interpretation; and the apparent meaning is also correct that the tie of kinship itself spoke, and in this realm, there is nothing preventing the tie of kinship from having a tongue.) So Allah the Exalted said, ""Yes. Are you not pleased that I will join with the one who joins you, and I will cut off from the one who cuts you off?"" The tie of kinship said, ""I am pleased with that."" So Allah the Exalted said, ""Then you have that rank."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, recite this verse: Allah the Exalted says to the hypocrites, ""If you gain authority, will you spread corruption in the land and sever the ties of kinship? Those are the ones whom Allah has cursed, so He made them deaf and blinded their eyes. Do they not reflect upon the Qur'an, or are there locks upon their hearts?"" (Muhammad: 22-24)."
"1765","Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: The one who severs the ties of kinship will not enter Paradise. Ibn Abi Umar said that Sufyan said: That is, the person who breaks family relations (will not enter Paradise)."
"1766","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who looks after an orphan, whether he is a relative or not, will be with me in Paradise like these two fingers. And Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) gestured with his index finger and middle finger."
"1767","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever earns and works for widows or for the poor, for him is a rank like that of one who fights in the way of Allah, and I think he (peace and blessings be upon him) also said: like the one who stands for prayer and does not tire, and like the fasting person who does not break his fast."
"1768","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah the Exalted will say on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who loved one another for My greatness and obedience? Today, I will shade them in My shade, and today there is no shade except My shade."
"1769","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: A man set out to visit his brother in another village, so Allah Almighty appointed an angel on his way. When he reached there, the angel asked him, ""Where are you going?"" He replied, ""I have a brother in that village; I am going to see him."" The angel asked, ""Is there any favor of his upon you which you are going to repay?"" He replied, ""No, he has no favor upon me; I only wish to see him for the sake of Allah."" So the angel said, ""Then I am a messenger from Allah, and Allah loves you as you love your brother for His (Allah's) sake."""
"1770","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) come?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""What have you prepared for the Hour?"" He replied, ""The love of Allah and His Messenger."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You will be with those whom you love."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""After embracing Islam, we were never as happy about anything as we were upon hearing this hadith."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I love Allah, His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), and I hope that I will be with them on the Day of Judgment, even though I have not done deeds like theirs."""
"1771","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, when Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibreel (peace be upon him) and says: “I love so-and-so, so you also love him.” Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) loves him, and then he announces in the heavens: “Allah loves so-and-so, so you all love him.” Then the inhabitants of the heavens love him. After that, acceptance is placed for him in the hearts of the people on earth. And when Allah is displeased with a person, He calls Jibreel (peace be upon him) and says: “I dislike so-and-so, so you also dislike him.” Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) dislikes him, and then he announces among the inhabitants of the heavens: “Allah dislikes so-and-so, so you all dislike him.” So they also dislike him, and then enmity for him is established among the people on earth (meaning that even the righteous servants or angels of Allah on earth remain his enemies)."
"1772","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in a marfu‘ form that` people are like mines of gold and silver. Those who were good in the time of ignorance are good in Islam as well, when they gain understanding of the religion. And souls are like gathered troops. Those among them who recognized each other are friends in this world as well, and those who were apart there, remain apart here too."
"1773","`Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A believer to (another) believer is like a building, one brick supports another (in the same way, it is necessary for one believer to be the helper of another believer)."
"1774","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The example of the believers in their mutual love, mercy, and compassion is like that of a single body; when any limb of it suffers, the whole body responds with sleeplessness and fever. (In the same way, when a calamity befalls a believer, especially one caused by the disbelievers, all believers should feel restless and strive to remedy it.)"
"1775","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not envy one another, do not artificially raise prices, do not harbor enmity against one another, and none of you should make a sale over the sale of his brother. And be, O servants of Allah, brothers to one another. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim: he does not wrong him, nor does he humiliate him, nor does he look down upon him. Piety and righteousness are here—and he (peace be upon him) pointed to his chest three times (meaning, a person is not truly pious by outward good deeds until his heart is pure). It is enough evil for a man to hold his Muslim brother in contempt. All things of a Muslim are forbidden for another Muslim: his blood, his wealth, and his honor."
"1776","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, Allah does not look at your appearances or your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds."
"1777","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When Allah conceals (the faults of) a servant in this world, He will also conceal (his faults) in the Hereafter. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Whoever conceals the fault of a servant in this world, Allah will conceal his fault (on the Day of Resurrection)."
"1778","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that when someone would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with a need, he (peace be upon him) would say to his companions: ""Intercede, you will be rewarded, and Allah will decide upon the tongue of His Prophet whatever He wills."""
"1779","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: The example of a good companion and a bad companion is like that of a musk seller and a blacksmith. The musk seller will either give you some as a gift, or you will buy some from him, or you will get a pleasant fragrance from him. As for the blacksmith, he will either burn your clothes, or you will have to smell a bad odor from him. (That is, the effects of good and bad companions are reflected upon a person.)"
"1780","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""Gabriel (peace be upon him) kept advising me to treat the neighbor well, to the extent that I thought he would make the neighbor an heir."""
"1781","`Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` my beloved friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me that when you cook meat, make the broth plentiful and look to the people of your neighbor's house and give them some of it."
"1782","`Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: Do not consider any act of kindness and goodness to be insignificant (that is, there is reward in every small or big act of kindness), and it is also an act of kindness that you meet your brother with a cheerful face."
"1783","`Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) used to say: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of goodness."
"1784","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Gentleness is not found in anything except that it beautifies it, and it is not removed from anything except that it makes it defective."
"1785","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aisha! Allah loves gentleness (and good character), and He Himself is gentle, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness or for anything else."
"1786","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Honor is Allah Almighty's lower garment and greatness is His cloak (meaning these are His attributes). Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says that whoever tries to take these away from Me, I will punish him."""
"1787","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will neither speak to three persons on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, nor will He look at them (with mercy), and for them is a painful punishment. The first is an old adulterer, the second is a lying king, and the third is an arrogant poor man."
"1788","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man said, ""By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so."" And Allah the Exalted said, ""Who is he who swears that I will not forgive so-and-so? I have forgiven him, and I have rendered all the deeds (of the one who swore) null and void."""
"1789","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give him permission, he is a bad person among his people."" When he entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to him gently. Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You said such about him, then you spoke to him gently."" So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Aisha! The worst person in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection will be the one whom people avoid because of his evil."""
"1790","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Charity does not decrease wealth, and whoever forgives, Allah increases his honor, and whoever humbles himself for the sake of Allah, Allah raises his status."
"1791","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whom do you consider to be childless? The people said: The one who does not have children (i.e., whose children do not survive). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He is not childless (his children will be there to help him in the Hereafter). Truly childless is the person who has not sent anything ahead from his children (i.e., none of his sons or daughters die before him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Well, whom do you count as a wrestler among you? We said: A wrestler is the one whom men cannot overpower. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, a wrestler is the one who controls himself at the time of anger (i.e., does not say anything against wisdom with his tongue and does not raise his hand against anyone)."
"1792","Sayedna Sulaiman bin Surad (may Allah be pleased with him) says that two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). One of them became angry and his face turned red. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I know a word, if this person says it, his anger will go away. That word is: (A‘udhu billahi min ash-shaytan ir-rajim)."" One of those who heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went and told the angry man what the Prophet had said. The man replied, ""Do you think I am mad?"""
"1793","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty made the figure of Adam (peace be upon him) in Paradise, He left it as long as He willed. Satan began to go around it and look at it. Then, when he saw it to be hollow from inside, he recognized that it had been created in such a way that it would not be able to restrain itself (i.e., it would not be able to control itself in desires, anger, and rage, or it would not be able to protect itself from whispers)."
"1794","Sayyiduna Nawas bin Sam'an (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in Madinah for a year (in the manner of someone who comes from another country to meet you and intends to return to his own country), and I did not migrate for this reason (i.e., I did not abandon the intention of returning to my country), because when any of us migrated, he would not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) anything (unlike travelers, who were allowed to ask). I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about good and evil, so he said: Goodness and virtue are good character, and sin is that which pricks your heart and you dislike that people should come to know of it."
"1795","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man saw a thorny branch on the road and said, ""By Allah! I will remove this from the path of the Muslims so that it does not harm them."" So Allah, the Exalted, admitted him into Paradise."
"1796","`Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I said, ""O Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Tell me something from which I may benefit."" So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims."""
"1797","Aswad says that some young men of the Quraysh went to Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) while she was in Mina, and they were laughing. Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) asked, ""Why are you laughing?"" They said that such-and-such a person fell on the tent rope and his neck or eye was barely saved. Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""Do not laugh, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said that if a Muslim is pricked by a thorn or suffers anything more than that, then for him a rank is raised and a sin of his is erased."""
"1798","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whenever a believer is afflicted with any hardship, pain, illness, or sorrow—even the worry that befalls him—his sins are erased because of it."
"1799","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: When this verse was revealed, ""Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it,"" it was very hard on the Muslims (that there would certainly be punishment for every sin). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Be moderate and seek the right path, and every affliction that befalls a Muslim is an expiation for his sins, even a stumble or a prick of a thorn (so that many sins are recompensed in this world, and it is hoped that there will be no reckoning in the Hereafter)."
"1800","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Do not harbor hatred against one another, do not envy one another, and do not show hostility to one another. Be, O servants of Allah, as brothers. And it is not permissible for any Muslim to abandon speaking to his brother for more than three days due to hatred."
"1801","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon speaking to his Muslim brother for more than three nights, such that when they meet, one turns his face this way and the other turns his face that way. And the better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace (salam)."
"1802","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of Paradise are opened on Mondays and Thursdays. Then every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except for the person who harbors enmity against his brother; his forgiveness is withheld, and it is said: ""Wait for these two until they reconcile. Wait for these two until they reconcile (when they reconcile, then they will be forgiven)."""
"1803","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the greatest falsehood. Do not listen to others’ conversations, do not spy, do not envy one another (except in matters of religion, which is permissible), do not be jealous, do not harbor malice, do not cut off relations, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers to one another."
"1804","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""Indeed, Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray in the Arabian Peninsula (as he was worshipped in the days of ignorance), but he is hopeful that he will incite discord among them (i.e., he will provoke them to fight among themselves)."""
"1805","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from her at night. So, I felt jealous (she thought that the Prophet, peace be upon him, had gone to another wife). Then the Prophet, peace be upon him, returned and saw my condition, so he said, “O Aisha! What has happened to you? Have you become jealous?” I said, “Why should I not be jealous when someone like me (a young, beautiful woman) has a husband like you?” The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, “Has your devil come to you?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Is there a devil with me?” He, peace be upon him, said, “Yes.” I said, “Is there a devil with every human being?” He, peace be upon him, said, “Yes.” Then I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Is there a devil with you too?” He, peace be upon him, said, “Yes, but my Lord has helped me against him until he has become submissive to me (so now he does not command me to do evil).”"
"1806","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what backbiting is? The people said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace be upon him) said: Backbiting is that you mention about your brother something which he would dislike (if he were present). The people said: O Messenger of Allah! What if that fault is actually present in our brother? He (peace be upon him) said: If that fault is in him, then you have backbitten him; and if it is not in him, then it is slander and false accusation."
"1807","‘Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that indeed Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: “Shall I not tell you what is the most heinous slander? It is tale-bearing which sows enmity among people.” And Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: “A person continues to speak the truth until he is recorded with Allah as truthful, and he continues to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a liar.”"
"1808","Hammam bin Harith says: We were sitting in the mosque with Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) when a man came and sat down with us. The people said to Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that this man conveys matters to the ruler. Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him), intending for him to hear, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise."""
"1809","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Adhere to truthfulness, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful person. And beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."
"1810","Narrated from Sayyida Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah bin Abi Mu’it (may Allah be pleased with her), and she was among the first emigrant women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good things with the intention of bringing about reconciliation.” Ibn Shihab said: “I have not heard that lying is permitted except in three cases: in war, in order to reconcile between people, and what a man says to his wife and a wife to her husband (for the sake of pleasantness).” And in another narration, she says: “I have not heard that lying is permitted except in three cases: (that is, in war, in order to reconcile between people, and what a man says to his wife and a wife to her husband) (for the sake of pleasantness).”"
"1811","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a battle when a Muhajir struck an Ansari on the buttocks (either with his hand or with a sword). The Ansari called out, ""O Ansar, come to help!"" and the Muhajir called out, ""O Muhajirin, come to help!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This is a call of the days of ignorance (Jahiliyyah)."" The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! A Muhajir struck an Ansari on the buttocks."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Leave this, for it is a filthy thing."" This news reached Abdullah bin Ubayy (the hypocrite), so he said, ""Did the Muhajirin do this? By Allah, when we return to Madinah, the honorable person among us will surely expel the lowly one from there."" (God forbid, this hypocrite considered himself honorable and called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lowly.) Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Leave him (O Umar)! Lest people say that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) kills his companions."" (Although that accursed one deserved it, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not punish him out of wisdom.)"
"1812","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When two people abuse each other, the sin will be upon the one who started it, as long as the oppressed does not exceed the limits."
"1813","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Man hurts Me; he says, ""Woe to the misfortune of time."" So none of you should say, ""Woe to the misfortune of time,"" because I am time; I bring the night and the day. When I wish, I will end the night and the day. (Since Allah Almighty is the Creator of night and day, to curse the night and day, that is, time, is in fact to curse Allah.)"
"1814","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah Himself is time (that is, time can do nothing; the One who acts is Allah alone)."
"1815","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should threaten his brother with a weapon, for he does not know, perhaps Satan may cause his hand to slip (and the weapon strikes), and thus he falls into a pit of Hell because of killing his brother."
"1816","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) instructed a person who was distributing arrows near the mosque that when he carries arrows, he should hold them by their pointed (i.e., sharp) end."
"1817","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When any one of you passes through the mosque or the market and has arrows in his hand, he should hold them by their tips. Then hold them by their tips, then hold them by their tips (he said this three times for emphasis). Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah, we did not die until we had placed the arrows at each other's faces. (That is, we fought among ourselves and acted against the instruction of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him.)"
"1818","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you fights with his brother, he should not strike him on the face."
"1819","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights with his brother, he should avoid striking his face, for Allah created man in His own image. (This attribution is an honorific, just as the Ka'bah is attributed to Allah, i.e., the House of Allah.)"
"1820","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey, and an Ansari woman was riding a she-camel. The she-camel became restless, so the woman cursed it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard this and said, ""Unload whatever is on this she-camel and leave her, for she is accursed."" Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""It is as if I am seeing that she-camel now, wandering about, and no one among the people paid any attention to her."""
"1821","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who curse others will neither intercede for anyone nor bear witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"1822","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` it was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray against the polytheists."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""I have not been sent to curse people, but rather I have been sent as a mercy (for them)."""
"1823","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When someone says (considering himself superior and others inferior) that people are ruined, then he himself is the most ruined of all. (And if he says it out of grief or sorrow over the corruption of religion, then it is not prohibited.) Abu Ishaq (Ibn Muhammad bin Sufyan) said: I do not know whether the word in the hadith is ""ahlak"" or ""ahlak""."
"1824","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Those who split hairs have perished (i.e., those who indulge in useless hair-splitting, go to extremes, and are bigoted). He said this three times."
"1825","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Two persons came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I do not know what they talked about with him, but he became angry and cursed them and spoke ill of them. When they went out, I said, “O Messenger of Allah! They will not benefit from anything.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Why?” I said, “Because you cursed them and spoke ill of them.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do you not know what I have stipulated with my Lord? I have said: O my Lord! I am a human being, so for any Muslim whom I curse or speak ill of, make it a purification and a reward for him.”"
"1826","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` there was an orphan girl with Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her), who was called Umm Anas. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw this girl and said: ""This girl has grown up; may Allah not prolong your life."" Upon hearing this, the girl went to Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) crying. Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) asked, ""Daughter, what happened to you?"" She replied, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has supplicated against me that my life may not be prolonged. Now I will never grow up,"" or she said, ""that your companion may not grow up."" Hearing this, Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) quickly put on her shawl and went out to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""What is it, Umm Sulaym?"" She said, ""O Noble Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Did you supplicate against my orphan girl?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""What supplication?"" She said, ""She says that you said her or her companion's life may not be prolonged."" Upon hearing this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and said, ""O Umm Sulaym! Do you not know that I have made a condition with my Lord? My condition is that I said: O Lord! I am a human being; I become pleased as a human becomes pleased and I become angry as a human becomes angry. So, for anyone from my Ummah upon whom I supplicate (against) undeservedly, then make it a means of purification, cleanliness, and nearness to You for him on the Day of Resurrection."" And Abu Ma'n has narrated in this hadith in all three places ""yateemah"" as ""yutayyimah"" with the diminutive form."
"1827","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says:` I was playing with children when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came. And I hid behind a door. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) patted me (affectionately) with his blessed hand and said, ""Go and call Muawiyah."" I went and then returned and said, ""He is eating."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) again said, ""Go and call Muawiyah."" I went again and returned and said, ""He is eating."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""May Allah not fill his stomach."" Ibn Musanna said: I asked Umayyah, ""What does 'Hatta' mean?"" He replied that it means the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) on the nape. (This hadith is also in the same meaning as mentioned in previous ahadith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made a condition with Allah that if he ever said something contrary to reality for someone, it would become a mercy for him. Therefore, this hadith is among the virtues of Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
